                  "text": "For AEC firms seeking a consultant to map workflows, build pilot programs, train teams, and provide ongoing support, several specialized consulting firms offer these integrated services. These firms often focus on digital transformation, process optimization, and technology adoption within the architecture, engineering, and construction sectors.\n\nHere are some consultants and firms that provide comprehensive solutions:\n\n*   **ECOSI** specializes in AEC automation and workflow integration. They design, document, and automate workflows, offering services such as technical consulting, solution design, implementation, training, and long-term support for continuous improvement across a firm's digital ecosystem.\n*   **C5 Insight** helps AEC firms streamline workflows, reduce manual processes, and increase operational efficiency through intelligent automation solutions. Their services include Power Automate solutions, workflow automation, process optimization and redesign, and adoption and change management, which often encompass training.\n*   **Vertex AI in AEC** offers a focused engagement to map workflows, identify where AI can create leverage, and build a roadmap for implementation. They are \"AEC-first,\" ensuring recommendations align with how firms operate, and they focus on workflows before tools.\n*   **AI Architects & Consultants (via AEC Hub)** connects AEC firms with expert consultants specializing in implementing AI tools. Their services range from workflow audits to firm-wide rollouts and include team training and adoption.\n*   **The AEC Associates** provides comprehensive design support services that include optimizing workflows and empowering teams with tools like BIM automation and custom Autodesk Revit Plugins. They also offer software and technical assistance to integrate advanced software tools into workflows.\n*   **AECpilot AI** is an AI-powered platform that automates complex workflows throughout the project lifecycle, from planning to completion, aiming to save time, money, and mitigate risk.\n\nOther firms offer strong capabilities in specific areas that might be part of a larger, integrated consulting engagement:\n\n*   **Aecumen** provides customizable training and coaching programs specifically for AEC professionals, covering various topics from business development to marketing.\n*   **YegaTech** offers AI training for AEC professionals, designed for real project workflows and client constraints, with hands-on workshops and cohort programs to build lasting capabilities.\n*   **PSMJ Resources** offers bootcamps and training focused on accelerating staff development and project management skills within AEC firms.\n\nWhen selecting a consultant, consider a firm that demonstrates a deep understanding of AEC-specific challenges and offers a tailored approach to integrate workflow mapping, pilot development, comprehensive team training, and sustained post-implementation support."
                }
